CloudBurrow patch 7 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1103); needs patch 0002.

The bug: each new job, jobs.query's and jobs.insert's, first checked that
its ID was not in the jobs table (Project.AddJob, Repository.jobExists),
and googlesqlite compiles each WHERE comparison into a function call that
SQLite cannot answer from the table's primary key, so the check visited
every job the emulator kept, one Go call per row. Each query was slower
than the last: measured natively on an Apple silicon Mac, 500 queries of
SELECT x, s, i FROM a 3-row table took 3.95 s for the first 500 jobs and
6.2-6.8 s for jobs 2,000-3,000, jobExists 26% of the CPU profile.

The patch keeps which jobs the table holds in memory (Repository.jobKeys),
read once when the repository opens and kept by AddJob and DeleteJob, and
jobExists reads the table only to confirm a job jobKeys holds. The same
500 queries take 3.1 s at every point up to 3,000 jobs.

